    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">25 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Grid BFS / DFS</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Multi-source from the border</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/pacific-atlantic-water-flow/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 417</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Pacific Atlantic Water Flow</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Do not ask every cell where its rain goes. Reverse the question: start at each ocean's edge and climb uphill (to cells at least as high). Two floods, one per ocean, and the answer is the cells both reach. O(m·n) time and space.</p>\n"
